{
  "id": "introduction-prononciation",
  "category": "introduction",
  "subgroup": null,
  "subgroup_label": "",
  "title": "🇸🇰 Introduction — Prononciation slovaque",
  "image": {
    "src": "img/1920px-Pronunciation_organs_diagram.png",
    "caption": "Diagramme des organes de prononciation — Wikimedia Commons"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "lines": [
        "Le slovaque se lit presque comme il s'écrit.",
        "Une fois les quelques lettres particulières maîtrisées, la prononciation devient beaucoup plus régulière qu'en français."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "1. Les accents et signes en slovaque"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "En français, les accents servent souvent à modifier une voyelle ou à distinguer des mots."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "En slovaque, les signes diacritiques font partie intégrante de l'alphabet : ils changent réellement le son."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Signe",
        "Nom français",
        "Nom slovaque",
        "Effet"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "´",
          "accent aigu",
          "dĺžeň",
          "allonge la voyelle"
        ],
        [
          "ˇ",
          "accent circonflexe inversé / caron",
          "mäkčeň",
          "rend la consonne \"douce\""
        ],
        [
          "¨",
          "tréma",
          "prehláska (familièrement \"dve bodky\")",
          "modifie la prononciation de certaines voyelles"
        ],
        [
          "ˆ",
          "accent circonflexe",
          "vokáň",
          "uniquement sur ô"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "2. Les voyelles"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Les voyelles slovaques peuvent être courtes ou longues."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Une voyelle longue dure environ deux fois plus longtemps."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Slovaque",
        "Exemple de mot slovaque",
        "Prononciation approximative"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "a",
          "mama",
          "a comme dans \"papa\""
        ],
        [
          "á",
          "krásny",
          "aa long"
        ],
        [
          "e",
          "deň",
          "è ouvert"
        ],
        [
          "é",
          "méta",
          "é long"
        ],
        [
          "i",
          "vidím",
          "i comme en français"
        ],
        [
          "í",
          "prší",
          "ii long"
        ],
        [
          "o",
          "dom",
          "o comme \"eau\""
        ],
        [
          "ó",
          "tón",
          "oo long"
        ],
        [
          "u",
          "ruka",
          "ou"
        ],
        [
          "ú",
          "múka",
          "ou long"
        ],
        [
          "y",
          "syn",
          "identique à i"
        ],
        [
          "ý",
          "dobrý",
          "identique à í"
        ],
        [
          "ä",
          "päť",
          "entre è et a (souvent proche de \"è\")"
        ],
        [
          "ô",
          "stôl",
          "\"uo\" prononcé rapidement"
        ]
      ],
      "speakable_column": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "3. Les consonnes particulières"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Slovaque",
        "Exemple de mot slovaque",
        "Prononciation approximative"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "č",
          "čas",
          "tch comme \"tchèque\""
        ],
        [
          "š",
          "škola",
          "ch comme \"chat\""
        ],
        [
          "ž",
          "žena",
          "j comme dans \"journal\""
        ],
        [
          "c",
          "cena",
          "ts comme \"tsar\""
        ],
        [
          "j",
          "ja",
          "y comme \"yaourt\""
        ],
        [
          "h",
          "hora",
          "h aspiré léger"
        ],
        [
          "ch",
          "chlieb",
          "racle de gorge comme en allemand \"Bach\""
        ],
        [
          "ď",
          "ďakujem",
          "d mouillé"
        ],
        [
          "ť",
          "deň / ťa",
          "t mouillé"
        ],
        [
          "ň",
          "kôň",
          "gn comme \"montagne\""
        ],
        [
          "ľ",
          "ľudia",
          "l mouillé"
        ],
        [
          "r",
          "ruka",
          "r roulé"
        ],
        [
          "ŕ",
          "vŕba",
          "r roulé long"
        ]
      ],
      "speakable_column": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "4. Sons importants à reconnaître"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Č = \"tch\""
    },
    {
      "type": "audio-card",
      "phrase": "čas",
      "speaker": null,
      "natural": "le temps",
      "literal": [
        "čas = temps"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Le č se prononce \"tch\", comme dans le mot français \"tchèque\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Š = \"ch\""
    },
    {
      "type": "audio-card",
      "phrase": "škola",
      "speaker": null,
      "natural": "l'école",
      "literal": [
        "škola = école"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Le š correspond au son \"ch\" du français."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Ž = \"j\""
    },
    {
      "type": "audio-card",
      "phrase": "žena",
      "speaker": null,
      "natural": "une femme",
      "literal": [
        "žena = femme"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Le ž correspond au son du \"j\" dans \"journal\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "C = \"ts\""
    },
    {
      "type": "audio-card",
      "phrase": "cena",
      "speaker": null,
      "natural": "le prix",
      "literal": [
        "cena = prix"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Le c n'est jamais prononcé comme un \"k\" ou un \"s\" : toujours \"ts\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "J = \"y\""
    },
    {
      "type": "audio-card",
      "phrase": "ja",
      "speaker": null,
      "natural": "moi / je",
      "literal": [
        "ja = moi"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Le j slovaque correspond toujours au son \"y\" français, jamais au \"j\" de \"jour\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "CH = son guttural"
    },
    {
      "type": "audio-card",
      "phrase": "chlieb",
      "speaker": null,
      "natural": "le pain",
      "literal": [
        "chlieb = pain"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Le son est proche du \"ch\" allemand dans \"Bach\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Ď, Ť, Ň, Ľ : les consonnes molles"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ces consonnes sont prononcées avec la langue proche du palais."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Slovaque",
        "Son proche"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "ď",
          "dy"
        ],
        [
          "ť",
          "ty"
        ],
        [
          "ň",
          "gn"
        ],
        [
          "ľ",
          "ly"
        ]
      ],
      "speakable_column": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "5. L'accent tonique"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "L'accent principal tombe presque toujours sur la première syllabe."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Mot",
        "Découpage"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Slovensko",
          "SLO-ven-sko"
        ],
        [
          "Bratislava",
          "BRA-ti-sla-va"
        ],
        [
          "ďakujem",
          "ĎA-ku-jem"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Contrairement au français, les syllabes gardent une longueur et une netteté assez régulières."
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "6. Pièges pour un francophone"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Les lettres qui ne se prononcent pas comme en français"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Lettre",
        "Français aurait tendance à dire",
        "Slovaque"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "j",
          "j de \"jour\"",
          "y de \"yaourt\""
        ],
        [
          "c",
          "k ou s",
          "ts"
        ],
        [
          "h",
          "souvent muet ou aspiré",
          "h prononcé"
        ],
        [
          "r",
          "r français",
          "r roulé"
        ],
        [
          "ch",
          "ch français",
          "son guttural"
        ]
      ],
      "speakable_column": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Le \"r\" slovaque"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Le r est roulé comme dans beaucoup de langues slaves."
    },
    {
      "type": "audio-card",
      "phrase": "ruka",
      "speaker": null,
      "natural": "la main",
      "literal": [
        "ruka = main"
      ],
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Pas de voyelles nasales"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Le français utilise :"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "an",
        "en",
        "on",
        "in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Le slovaque ne les utilise pas."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Français",
        "Slovaque"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "bon",
          "bon + voyelle prononcée"
        ],
        [
          "sans",
          "s-a-n-s"
        ],
        [
          "vin",
          "v-i-n"
        ]
      ],
      "speakable_column": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "hr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "7. Petit entraînement de lecture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Lire lentement, en posant chaque son :"
    },
    {
      "type": "audio-card",
      "phrase": "Dobrý deň, ako sa máte? Ďakujem, dobre.",
      "speaker": null,
      "natural": "Bonjour, comment allez-vous ? Merci, ça va bien.",
      "literal": [
        "Dobrý deň = bonjour",
        "ako sa máte = comment vous portez-vous",
        "Ďakujem, dobre = merci, bien"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Une bonne phrase pour s'entraîner : elle contient dĺžeň (á, ý), mäkčeň (ď) et l'accent tonique sur la première syllabe de chaque mot."
      ]
    }
  ]
}